r accomplished by one continuous movement or not\". \"semicircular turn\": a turn through a half circle reverses the direction of travel, the observable the U-turn concept recognizes, so it is read by drv.motion.u_turn. Alternative acts sharing one occasion."},{"span":"d7","atoms":["st.median_or_divider","rel.occupies"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"through an opening\": ego's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) a median or divider of h whose opening attribute is set ('opening attribute where a crossover exists') at some moment of the turn: a turn made through an opening passes through it, it is not inside it throughout."},{"span":"d8","atoms":["st.median_or_divider","st.intersection","rel.occupies"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"a crossover\": a median or divider of h with the opening attribute; \"intersection\": ego's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) an st.intersection lying on h at some moment of the turn. \"established by a public authority\": status read through the feature's presence."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"Ego is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; driven: agency reading); at the judged observation ego's left turn (drv.motion.left_turn with p.turn_window, p.left_turn_min_angle, p.left_turn_max_angle) or U-turn (drv.motion.u_turn with p.turn_window, p.u_turn_min_angle, p.u_turn_max_angle) is recognized (the concept rises), and at some observation while it was under way ego's footprint overlapped (rel.occupies) a roadway (st.roadway) or a median or divider lying on a highway h on which a median or divider lies (st.on_way, st.highway, st.median_or_divider).","obligation":"Violated at that recognition unless, at some observation while the turn was under way, ego's footprint overlapped a median or divider of h with the opening attribute set, or an intersection lying on h (st.intersection, st.on_way); compliant where it did.","params":["p.turn_window","p.left_turn_min_angle","p.left_turn_max_angle","p.u_turn_min_angle","p.u_turn_max_angle","p.turn_yaw_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"d2","why":"'driven' is read through ego's controlled motion: a vehicle on the road is taken to be driven.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"d8","why":"'established by a public authority' is read through the presence of the crossover or intersection on the road.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Ego, on the right-hand roadway of a divided highway, turns left across the solid median, where no opening exists, into a driveway on the far side; its left turn is recognized and at no moment of it did ego overlap an opening or an intersection."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Ego makes a left turn at an intersection of the divided highway; its footprint overlaps the intersection during the turn."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"Ego makes a left turn from a two-way road whose highway carries no median or divider."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Scene of forbid, but the source declares kin.yaw_rate absent: whether ego turned cannot be read.","masked":["kin.yaw_rate"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"Ego reverses direction mid-block on a divided highway by a multi-point U-turn across the median where no opening exists."},{"name":"occasion_d2","expected":"violated","narrative":"Ego is on a roadway of the divided highway during the first part of its left turn only, then crosses into a side driveway; at no moment of the turn did it overlap an opening or an intersection."},{"name":"occasion_d2_outside","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"Ego left the divided highway onto an undivided street before its turn began, then made a left turn there; during the turn it is on no region of a divided highway."},{"name":"occasion_d7","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Ego makes a left turn across the median through an opening: during part of the turn its footprint overlaps the median region with the opening attribute set."},{"name":"occasion_d7_outside","expected":"violated","narrative":"Ego passed through a median opening before its turn began; the turn itself crosses the median where no opening exists and no intersection lies."},{"name":"occasion_d8","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Ego makes a U-turn whose middle part lies within an intersection of the divided highway."},{"name":"occasion_d8_outside","expected":"violated","narrative":"Ego was in an intersection of the divided highway only before its U-turn began; it makes the U-turn mid-block across a median with no opening."}],"occasion":{"act":["drv.motion.left_turn","drv.motion.u_turn"],"boundary":"window","window":"p.turn_window","under_way":{"words":"make any left turn, semicircular turn or U-turn","atoms":["kin.yaw_rate"],"derived":[],"justification":"Within the window behind the recognition, the turn is under way from the first observation at which the magnitude of ego's yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate) is at or above p.turn_yaw_tolerance to the recognition; before it ego's heading was not changing at that rate. This reads ego's motion, not a region it occupies."},"spans":{"d2":"some_moment","d7":"some_moment","d8":"some_moment"}},"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.turn_window","unit":"s","value":15.0,"convention":"Window within which a turn at a junction or across a median, including a U-turn made in several movements, is completed.","source":"Turning-movement durations in naturalistic intersection data (single turns of a few seconds; multi-point U-turns longer)."},{"name":"p.left_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a turn: a leftward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"Turning-movement classification in trajectory datasets (inD, NGSIM intersection data)."},{"name":"p.left_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Upper bound of a left turn, above which the direction of travel counts as reversed (a U-turn).","source":"Turning-movement classification in trajectory datasets (inD, NGSIM intersection data)."},{"name":"p.u_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Heading change at or beyond which the direction of travel counts as reversed.","source":"Turning-movement classification in trajectory datasets (inD, NGSIM intersection data)."},{"name":"p.u_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":210.0,"convention":"Heading change beyond which the road user has turned past the opposite direction (a loop rather than a reversal).","source":"Turning-movement classification in trajectory datasets (inD, NGSIM intersection data)."},{"name":"p.turn_yaw_tolerance","unit":"deg/s","value":5.0,"convention":"Yaw rate below which a change of heading counts as none: above lane-keeping yaw noise, below the yaw rates of turning at a junction.","source":"Vehicle-dynamics practice for turn-onset detection from yaw-rate sensors."}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_250_4_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-250-4"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"a1","text":"When a vehicle enters an intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a2","text":"controlled by a traffic-control signal which is installed and has its vehicular signals uncovered,","role":"condition"},{"id":"a3","text":"but is inoperative at the time the vehicle enters the intersection,","role":"condition"},{"id":"a4","text":"the driver of the vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"a5","text":"shall proceed as if a stop sign had been erected at each entrance to the intersection and shall stop","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a6","text":"at a clearly marked stop line","role":"condition"},{"id":"a7","text":"or, if there is none, before entering the crosswalk on the near side of the intersection","role":"condition"},{"id":"a8","text":"or, if there is none, at the point nearest the intersection where the driver has a view of approaching traffic on the through highway.","role":"condition"},{"id":"a9","text":"After making such a stop,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a10","text":"the driver","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a11","text":"shall proceed cautiously,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a12","text":"yielding to vehicles","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a13","text":"which have previously completed a stop or are within the intersection.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"a1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.intersection","st.travel_region","st.lane_enters","rel.occupies"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"a vehicle\": the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle. \"enters an intersection\": the observation at which ego's footprint comes to overlap (rel.occupies) an intersection i (st.intersection, 'the region where two roadways meet'), having occupied at the observation before, and not overlapping i, a carrier c (a travel region of a kind st.lane_enters admits) whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters, 'the intersection region a directed approach carrier runs into at its entrance end'); never inferred from distance or heading."},{"span":"a2","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal","dev.governs"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"traffic-control signal\" (DEF-NRS-484A-290 'any official traffic-control device ... by which traffic is alternately directed to stop or proceed'): a dev.traffic_signal head, 'a signal head', not a pedestrian head, which is no vehicular signal. \"controlled by\": the head governs (dev.governs, 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection') the intersection i or ego's approach carrier c; dev.governs is not a position. \"installed and has its vehicular signals uncovered\": the head is present with its uncovered attribute ('uncovered attribute for an installed head whose faces are not covered'); its official status is read through its presence."},{"span":"a3","atoms":["dev.inoperative"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.inoperative: 'a signal head installed and uncovered but showing no valid indication', exactly the words. \"at the time the vehicle enters\": read at the entry observation. The signal is inoperative where every head governing c or i is inoperative there, and at least one such head exists."},{"span":"a4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"the vehicle\": the same vehicle as a1 (admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle); \"the driver\" read through its controlled motion (agency reading)."},{"span":"a5","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"\"shall stop\": a stop when required, DEF-NRS-484A-255 \"complete cessation from movement\" (DEF-NRS-484A-260 governs a stop 'when prohibited' and does not apply to a required stop): drv.motion.at_rest. \"proceed as if a stop sign had been erected at each entrance\": ego owes at its own entrance what a stop-sign approach owes, the halt this node judges at the place a6-a8 name and the yield its sibling NRS_484B_250_4_o2 judges; the signs at the other entrances bind the other vehicles, each judged as its own subject."},{"span":"a6","atoms":["st.stop_line","st.entrance_of","st.region_geometry","st.lane_direction","prim.region_offset_along"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.stop_line, 'the transverse line marking where vehicles halt for a device', tied to ego's approach carrier c by st.entrance_of ('the carrier whose entrance into an intersection a stop line or a crosswalk marks'), never by distance. \"at\" the line: ego's body within p.stop_point_tolerance of it (st.region_geometry distance) and not past it, the side read along c's designated direction (st.lane_direction, sign of prim.region_offset_along), as the ontology's approach convention states. \"clearly marked\": the represented line is read as the clearly marked one (status reading)."},{"span":"a7","atoms":["st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.region_geometry","rel.occupies","st.lane_direction","prim.region_offset_along"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"if there is none\": the source's list of stop lines marking c is complete and none marks it. \"the crosswalk on the near side\": the st.crosswalk marking c (st.entrance_of), the crossing ego reaches first. \"before entering\": ego halts short of it with its footprint not overlapping it (rel.occupies false), within p.stop_point_tolerance outside it (st.region_geometry), side read along c (st.lane_direction, prim.region_offset_along)."},{"span":"a8","atoms":["st.intersection","st.region_geometry","rel.occupies","st.lane_enters"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"if there is none\": neither a stop line nor a crosswalk marks c (lists complete). \"the point nearest the intersection\": c's entrance end at i (st.lane_enters); the halt counts there where ego's footprint does not overlap i (rel.occupies false) and its body lies within p.stop_point_tolerance of i (st.region_geometry). \"where the driver has a view of approaching traffic on the through highway\": a perception, read through the place it secures (perception reading): the point nearest the intersection is its edge, from which the view of the crossing way is widest."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"Ego is a vehicle (driven: agency reading) and the judged observation is an entry of ego into an intersection i: ego's footprint overlaps i (rel.occupies, st.intersection) and at the observation before it did not, and occupied a carrier c whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters); at that entry at least one traffic signal head (dev.traffic_signal) governs c or i (dev.governs) and every such head is inoperative (dev.inoperative).","obligation":"Event and target: the entry of ego into i through c described in the applicability. Place: the stop line marking c (st.stop_line, st.entrance_of) where one is recorded; else, where the source's list for c is complete and no stop line marks it, the crosswalk marking c (st.crosswalk, st.entrance_of), a halt there being short of it with ego's footprint not overlapping it; else the entrance end of c at i, a halt there being outside i. A halt counts at the place where ego is at rest (drv.motion.at_rest, p.rest_speed_tolerance) on c with its body within p.stop_point_tolerance of the place (st.region_geometry) and not past it, the side read along c's designated direction (st.lane_direction, sign of prim.region_offset_along). Search: from the entry back to the approach start, the last observation before the entry at which ego, on a carrier the place marks, is outside the place's stopping zone upstream (off the place, short of it along c's direction and farther from it than p.stop_point_tolerance), or back to ego's previous entry into i, whichever comes first; nothing else ends it, not the start of the recording, not ego's first observation, not a distance travelled. Only an observed exit from the stopping zone upstream begins a new approach; crossing the place, a lateral move, a change of carrier within the same entry or a reverse within the zone does not, and none loses a halt already made. Verdict: compliant where the search finds such a halt; violated where it reaches the approach start or the previous entry without one; unknown where it reaches neither (the approach began before the recording), where whether the entry occurred is unknown (no observation of ego before it, ego on no mapped carrier, or c's association with the place unobserved), where which place governs turns on an unobserved association or an incomplete list, or where the signal's state at the entry is unobserved.","params":["p.rest_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"a4","why":"'the driver' is read through ego's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"a6","why":"'clearly marked' is read through the presence of the represented stop line; the paint's clarity is not modelled and the reading relaxes no choice of place.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"a8","why":"'where the driver has a view of approaching traffic on the through highway' is read through the place it secures: the point nearest the intersection, the entrance end of ego's approach carrier, outside the intersection.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"perception"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"The single traffic signal head governing ego's approach lane c is installed, uncovered and inoperative; a stop line marks c. Ego approaches from beyond the stopping zone and enters the intersection without being at rest at any observation since the approach start."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; ego comes to rest within p.stop_point_tolerance of the stop line, short of it, then enters."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The signal governing c shows circular_green when ego enters; it is not inoperative."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Scene of forbid, but the source declares dev.inoperative absent: whether the signal is inoperative at the entry cannot be read.","masked":["dev.inoperative"]},{"name":"history_boundary","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Signal inoperative; a stop line marks c. The recording begins with ego already within the stopping zone of the line moving slowly; ego enters without being at rest at any recorded observation. The approach start lies before the recording and no previous entry is recorded.","boundary":"the approach start: the observation at which ego, on c, was last outside the stop line's stopping zone upstream, which precedes the recording"},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"No stop line marks c (list complete); a crosswalk marks c. Ego comes to rest with its footprint overlapping the crosswalk, then enters; it was at rest nowhere short of the crosswalk."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Neither a stop line nor a crosswalk marks c (lists complete). Ego comes to rest outside the intersection within p.stop_point_tolerance of its edge, then enters."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement.","source":"Naturalistic-driving and simulator stop-detection practice (SHRP 2 event coding; CARLA ground-truth velocity resolution)."},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Stop-point tolerance of the ontology's approach convention: the body-to-mark distance within which a halt counts as made at the mark, and beyond which the road user is outside the stopping zone.","source":"MUTCD (2009) Section 3B.16 stop line placement; positioning accuracy of stop-compliance studies."}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_250_4_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-250-4"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"a1","text":"When a vehicle enters an intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a2","text":"controlled by a traffic-control signal which is installed and has its vehicular signals uncovered,","role":"condition"},{"id":"a3","text":"but is inoperative at the time the vehicle enters the intersection,","role":"condition"},{"id":"a4","text":"the driver of the vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"a5","text":"shall proceed as if a stop sign had been erected at each entrance to the intersection and shall stop","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a6","text":"at a clearly marked stop line","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a7","text":"or, if there is none, before entering the crosswalk on the near side of the intersection","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a8","text":"or, if there is none, at the point nearest the intersection where the driver has a view of approaching traffic on the through highway.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a9","text":"After making such a stop,","role":"condition"},{"id":"a10","text":"the driver","role":"subject"},{"id":"a11","text":"shall proceed cautiously,","role":"standard"},{"id":"a12","text":"yielding to vehicles","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a13","text":"which have previously completed a stop or are within the intersection.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"a1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.intersection","st.travel_region","st.lane_enters","rel.occupies"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"a vehicle\": the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle. \"enters an intersection\": the observation at which ego's footprint comes to overlap (rel.occupies) an intersection i (st.intersection), having occupied at the observation before a carrier c whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters); read through a past operator, since the judged observations follow it."},{"span":"a2","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal","dev.governs"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"traffic-control signal\": a dev.traffic_signal head ('a signal head') governing (dev.governs) i or c; installed and uncovered: present with its uncovered attribute. Not a pedestrian head."},{"span":"a3","atoms":["dev.inoperative"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.inoperative: 'a signal head installed and uncovered but showing no valid indication', read at the observation of ego's entry into i (\"at the time the vehicle enters\"), through a past operator: every head governing c or i inoperative there, at least one."},{"span":"a4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"the vehicle\": ego (admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle); \"the driver\" read through its controlled motion (agency reading)."},{"span":"a9","atoms":["st.stop_line","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.region_geometry","rel.occupies","st.lane_direction","prim.region_offset_along"],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"\"such a stop\" is the stop a5-a8 require, carried in full: ego at rest (drv.motion.at_rest, \"complete cessation from movement\") on its approach carrier c at the governing place, the stop line marking c (st.stop_line, st.entrance_of), else short of the crosswalk marking c with its footprint not overlapping it (st.crosswalk, rel.occupies), else outside i at c's entrance end, body within p.stop_point_tolerance of the place (st.region_geometry), side read along c (st.lane_direction, prim.region_offset_along), found between the approach start and ego's entry into i as NRS_484B_250_4_o1 states. A halt elsewhere is not such a stop. \"After\": the judged observations follow that halt."},{"span":"a10","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"the driver\": of ego, a vehicle (admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), read through its controlled motion (agency reading)."},{"span":"a12","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"\"yielding\": granting precedence: ego does not proceed while a vehicle it yields to is in conflict with it, so at every judged observation ego is at rest (drv.motion.at_rest) or not in conflict with that vehicle (operationalization of a11). \"vehicles\": road users of the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle other than ego."},{"span":"a13","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"\"are within the intersection\": b's footprint overlaps i (rel.occupies, st.intersection). \"have previously completed a stop\": b, on a carrier c_b other than c whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters), came to rest there (drv.motion.at_rest) and the rest it came to began before ego's halt on c began, and b still occupies c_b; once b enters i it is within the intersection."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"a11","standard":"proceed cautiously","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_clearance"],"convention":"Traffic-conflict technique: ego proceeds cautiously toward a vehicle it yields to where, projected at their current velocities, their centres do not approach within the time-to-collision horizon to a distance below the clearance at which their bodies would touch; the positions and velocities enter by degree.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"Ego is a vehicle (driven: agency reading) that entered an intersection i from a carrier c (st.lane_enters) at an observation at which at least one traffic signal head governed c or i (dev.traffic_signal, dev.governs) and every such head was inoperative (dev.inoperative), and that made, between the approach start and that entry, the stop a9 describes at the governing place on c (drv.motion.at_rest, p.rest_speed_tolerance, p.stop_point_tolerance); judged at every observation from that entry while ego's footprint overlaps i (rel.occupies). Where the history the stop's search needs precedes the recording, the applicability is unknown.","obligation":"For every vehicle b other than ego that overlaps i, or that occupies a carrier c_b other than c whose entrance end is i and came to rest there (drv.motion.at_rest) at an onset of rest earlier than the onset of ego's halt on c: ego is at rest (drv.motion.at_rest) or not in conflict with b, that is not both prim.closest_approach_within(ego, b) with horizon p.conflict_horizon and prim.closest_approach_distance(ego, b) with the same horizon below p.conflict_clearance.","params":["p.rest_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance","p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_clearance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"a4","why":"'the driver' is read through ego's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"a11","why":"'cautiously' is read through the conflict with the vehicles ego yields to: ego proceeds without a projected closest approach to such a vehicle below the clearance within the horizon; caution toward other road users is not read by this rule.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"a12","why":"A vehicle with precedence that keeps waiting at its own entrance is not in conflict with ego; ego proceeding while it waits is not read as a failure to yield.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"The signal governing ego's approach c is inoperative. Ego comes to rest at the stop line marking c, then enters the intersection while a vehicle b that is already within the intersection crosses ego's path; projected at constant velocities their centres approach within p.conflict_horizon below p.conflict_clearance while ego moves."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; ego stays at rest at the line until b has cleared the intersection, then proceeds with no projected conflict."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The signal governing c shows circular_red then circular_green; it is not inoperative when ego enters."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Scene of forbid, but the source declares dev.inoperative absent.","masked":["dev.inoperative"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"Signal inoperative. Vehicle b came to rest at its own stop line before ego came to rest at ego's line; b then moves toward the intersection while ego enters, and their projected closest approach falls below the clearance within the horizon."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Signal inoperative; ego stops at the line and crosses with no other road user in the scene."},{"name":"branch_3","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"As forbid, except that ego's only halt was far upstream of the stop line, outside its stopping zone, and ego did not halt at the line: no such stop was made, so this duty does not arise (NRS_484B_250_4_o1 judges the missing halt)."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement.","source":"Naturalistic-driving and simulator stop-detection practice (SHRP 2 event coding; CARLA ground-truth velocity resolution)."},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Stop-point tolerance of the ontology's approach convention: the body-to-mark distance within which a halt counts as made at the mark.","source":"MUTCD (2009) Section 3B.16 stop line placement; positioning accuracy of stop-compliance studies."},{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"Time-to-collision horizon of the traffic-conflict technique.","source":"Hayward (1972) time-to-collision; Hyden (1987) Swedish Traffic Conflict Technique; van der Horst (1990) TTC thresholds."},{"name":"p.conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Centre-to-centre distance at the projected closest approach below which the bodies of two passenger vehicles would touch or nearly touch.","source":"AASHTO Green Book, design vehicle P dimensions."}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_250_1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-250-1"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"e1","text":"The driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"e2","text":"approaching an intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e3","text":"shall yield","role":"obligation"},{"id":"e4","text":"the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"e5","text":"to a vehicle which has entered the intersection from a different highway.","role":"condition"},{"id":"e6","text":"Except as otherwise provided in subsection 4 [NRS-484B-250-4],","role":"reference"},{"id":"e7","text":"this section does not apply at intersections controlled by official traffic-control devices","role":"exception"},{"id":"e8","text":"or to vehicles approaching each other from opposite directions,","role":"exception"},{"id":"e9","text":"when the driver of one of the vehicles is intending to","role":"exception"},{"id":"e10","text":"or is making a left turn.","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"e1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"a vehicle\": the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; \"The driver\" read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency reading)."},{"span":"e2","atoms":["st.intersection","st.travel_region","st.lane_enters","rel.occupies"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"approaching an intersection\": ego occupies (rel.occupies) a carrier c whose entrance end is the intersection i (st.lane_enters: 'a road user occupying one such carrier approaches through it whatever its motion') and does not overlap i, or enters i at the judged observation from such a c. Not inferred from heading or distance."},{"span":"e3","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"\"yield\": granting precedence (DEF-NRS-484A-210 \"unless one grants precedence to the other\"): ego does not proceed while the vehicle with the right-of-way is in conflict with it, so ego is at rest (drv.motion.at_rest) or not in conflict (operationalization of e4)."},{"span":"e5","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.on_way","st.highway"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"a vehicle\": a road user b other than ego of the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle. \"has entered the intersection\": b's footprint overlaps i (rel.occupies) after an entry from a carrier c_b whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters), read through a past operator. \"from a different highway\": c_b lies (st.on_way) on a highway (st.highway) on which ego's carrier c does not lie; the intersection itself lies on every way that meets there and is no evidence of either."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"e4","standard":"the right-of-way: DEF-NRS-484A-210 \"approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other\"","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_clearance"],"convention":"Traffic-conflict technique: two road users are in conflict where, projected at their current velocities, their centres approach within the time-to-collision horizon and their closest-approach centre distance is below the clearance at which their bodies would touch. Direction, speed and proximity enter by degree through the projected velocities and positions.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[{"span":"e9","id":"int.left_turn","meaning":"The road user's current plan includes turning left at the target region."}],"compositions":[{"span":"e6","rule":"NRS_484B_250_4_o1","map":{"ego":"ego"},"as":"unless","scopes":"e7"},{"span":"e6","rule":"NRS_484B_250_4_o2","map":{"ego":"ego"},"as":"unless","scopes":"e7"}],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"Ego is a vehicle (driven: agency reading) approaching an intersection i (on a carrier c whose entrance end is i, not overlapping i, or entering i from c at the judged observation); and no traffic signal, stop sign or yield sign governs i or any carrier entering i (dev.traffic_signal, dev.stop_sign, dev.yield_sign, dev.governs, st.lane_enters), this exception being suspended where NRS_484B_250_4_o1 or NRS_484B_250_4_o2 applies to ego.","obligation":"For every vehicle b other than ego whose footprint overlaps i after an entry from a carrier c_b lying on a highway on which c does not lie (st.on_way): not where c and c_b carry opposed directions (st.lane_direction, the dot product of the two directions below minus p.opposite_direction_tolerance) and ego or b declares int.left_turn at i or is turning left (drv.motion.turning_left with p.turn_yaw_tolerance and p.rest_speed_tolerance); otherwise ego is at rest (drv.motion.at_rest, p.rest_speed_tolerance) or not in conflict with b: not both prim.closest_approach_within(ego, b) with horizon p.conflict_horizon and prim.closest_approach_distance(ego, b) with the same horizon below p.conflict_clearance.","params":["p.rest_speed_tolerance","p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_clearance","p.opposite_direction_tolerance","p.turn_yaw_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"e1","why":"'The driver' is read through ego's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"e7","why":"'official' is read through the presence of the device governing the intersection or an approach to it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"No device governs the intersection or its approaches. Ego approaches on highway A; vehicle b has entered from highway B and is crossing; ego keeps moving and enters while their projected closest approach lies within p.conflict_horizon below p.conflict_clearance."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; ego slows and comes to rest at the edge of the intersection until b has cleared, then enters with no projected conflict."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"Stop signs govern the approaches of highway B: the intersection is controlled by official traffic-control devices, and no inoperative signal is involved."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Scene of forbid, but the source declares st.lane_enters absent: whether ego approaches the intersection cannot be read.","masked":["st.lane_enters"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"No device governs the intersection. Vehicle b entered from the opposite approach of ego's own highway A; no vehicle from a different highway is within the intersection; ego enters."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"violated","narrative":"An inoperative traffic signal governs the intersection (NRS_484B_250_4_o1 applies to ego's entry), so the device exception is suspended; ego enters in conflict with b, which entered from highway B."},{"name":"branch_3","expected":"compliant","narrative":"No device governs the intersection and ego approaches and enters with no other road user in the scene."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement.","source":"Naturalistic-driving and simulator stop-detection practice (SHRP 2 event coding; CARLA ground-truth velocity resolution)."},{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"Time-to-collision horizon of the traffic-conflict technique.","source":"Hayward (1972) time-to-collision; Hyden (1987) Swedish Traffic Conflict Technique; van der Horst (1990) TTC thresholds."},{"name":"p.conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Centre-to-centre distance at the projected closest approach below which the bodies of two passenger vehicles would touch or nearly touch.","source":"AASHTO Green Book, design vehicle P dimensions."},{"name":"p.opposite_direction_tolerance","unit":"1","value":0.866,"convention":"Cosine of the largest angle off exactly opposed at which two approach directions still count as opposite (thirty degrees), covering skewed approaches.","source":"Trajectory-processing conventions for opposing-movement classification at intersections (inD)."},{"name":"p.turn_yaw_tolerance","unit":"deg/s","value":5.0,"convention":"Yaw rate below which a change of heading counts as none: above lane-keeping yaw noise, below the yaw rates of turning at a junction.","source":"Vehicle-dynamics practice for turn-onset detection from yaw-rate sensors."}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_253_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-253"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"f1","text":"The driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"f2","text":"within an intersection","role":"condition"},{"id":"f3","text":"intending to turn to the left","role":"condition"},{"id":"f4","text":"shall yield","role":"obligation"},{"id":"f5","text":"the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"f6","text":"to any vehicle approaching from the opposite direction","role":"condition"},{"id":"f7","text":"which is within the intersection","role":"condition"},{"id":"f8","text":"or so close thereto as to constitute an immediate hazard,","role":"standard"},{"id":"f9","text":"but such driver,","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"f10","text":"having so yielded","role":"sibling"},{"id":"f11","text":"and having given a signal when and as required,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"f12","text":"may make such left turn","role":"sibling"},{"id":"f13","text":"and the drivers of all other vehicles approaching the intersection from the opposite direction","role":"sibling"},{"id":"f14","text":"shall yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"f15","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"f16","text":"to the vehicle making the left turn.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"f1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"a vehicle\": the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; \"The driver\" read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency reading)."},{"span":"f2","atoms":["st.intersection","rel.occupies"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"within an intersection\": ego's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) an intersection i (st.intersection, 'the region where two roadways meet'); i is the region the intention f3 is declared at."},{"span":"f4","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"\"yield\": granting precedence (DEF-NRS-484A-210 \"unless one grants precedence to the other\"): ego does not proceed while the vehicle with the right-of-way is in conflict with it, so ego is at rest (drv.motion.at_rest) or not in conflict (operationalization of f5)."},{"span":"f6","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.lane_enters","st.lane_direction","st.travel_region","rel.occupies"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"any vehicle\": every road user b other than ego of the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle. \"approaching from the opposite direction\": read, as rel.oncoming's contract directs, through the carriers: b's approach carrier (the carrier whose entrance end is i that b occupies, or the one from which it entered i; st.lane_enters, rel.occupies) and ego's (the carrier from which ego entered i) carry opposed designated directions (st.lane_direction), not through the current headings, which a turn changes."},{"span":"f7","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"which is within the intersection\": b's footprint overlaps the same i (rel.occupies)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"f5","standard":"the right-of-way: DEF-NRS-484A-210 \"approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other\"","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_clearance"],"convention":"Traffic-conflict technique: two road users are in conflict where, projected at their current velocities, their centres approach within the time-to-collision horizon and their closest-approach centre distance is below the clearance at which their bodies would touch. Direction, speed and proximity enter by degree through the projected velocities and positions.","surrogate":false},{"span":"f8","standard":"so close thereto as to constitute an immediate hazard","concepts":["st.region_geometry","kin.speed"],"params":["p.immediate_hazard_time"],"convention":"Gap acceptance: an approaching vehicle is an immediate hazard where its time to reach the intersection is below the critical headway for a left turn, read as the ground distance from its body to the intersection (st.region_geometry) at or below its speed (kin.speed) times the critical headway; distance and speed enter by degree.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[{"span":"f3","id":"int.left_turn","meaning":"The road user's current plan includes turning left at the target region."}],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"Ego is a vehicle (driven: agency reading) whose footprint overlaps an intersection i (rel.occupies, st.intersection) and which declares int.left_turn at i at the judged observation.","obligation":"For every vehicle b other than ego whose approach to i is opposite to ego's (b's approach carrier, the carrier entering i that b occupies or the one from which it entered i, and the carrier from which ego entered i carry directions whose dot product is below minus p.opposite_direction_tolerance; st.lane_direction, st.lane_enters) and that either overlaps i or occupies its approach carrier with the ground distance from its body to i (st.region_geometry) at or below its speed (kin.speed) times p.immediate_hazard_time: ego is at rest (drv.motion.at_rest, p.rest_speed_tolerance) or not in conflict with b, that is not both prim.closest_approach_within(ego, b) with horizon p.conflict_horizon and prim.closest_approach_distance(ego, b) with the same horizon below p.conflict_clearance.","params":["p.rest_speed_tolerance","p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_clearance","p.immediate_hazard_time","p.opposite_direction_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"f1","why":"'The driver' is read through ego's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Ego is within the intersection and declares int.left_turn there. An oncoming vehicle b on the opposite approach is at a distance from the intersection below its speed times p.immediate_hazard_time; ego moves across b's path and their projected closest approach falls within p.conflict_horizon below p.conflict_clearance."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; ego stays at rest in the intersection until b has passed, then turns."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"Ego is within the intersection with a declared plan to go straight (int.left_turn false)."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Scene of forbid, but the source declares st.lane_direction absent: whether b approaches from the opposite direction cannot be read.","masked":["st.lane_direction"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Ego, within the intersection with int.left_turn, turns left with no other road user in the scene."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"compliant","narrative":"An oncoming vehicle b is on the opposite approach at a distance above its speed times p.immediate_hazard_time and not within the intersection; ego turns."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement.","source":"Naturalistic-driving and simulator stop-detection practice (SHRP 2 event coding; CARLA ground-truth velocity resolution)."},{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"Time-to-collision horizon of the traffic-conflict technique.","source":"Hayward (1972) time-to-collision; Hyden (1987) Swedish Traffic Conflict Technique; van der Horst (1990) TTC thresholds."},{"name":"p.conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Centre-to-centre distance at the projected closest approach below which the bodies of two passenger vehicles would touch or nearly touch.","source":"AASHTO Green Book, design vehicle P dimensions."},{"name":"p.immediate_hazard_time","unit":"s","value":4.1,"convention":"Critical headway of gap acceptance: an approaching vehicle whose time to reach the intersection is below it is too close for a turning or crossing manoeuvre to be completed ahead of it.","source":"Highway Capacity Manual, 6th ed., base critical headway for a major-street left turn."},{"name":"p.opposite_direction_tolerance","unit":"1","value":0.866,"convention":"Cosine of the largest angle off exactly opposed at which two approach directions still count as opposite (thirty degrees).","source":"Trajectory-processing conventions for opposing-movement classification at intersections (inD)."}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_253_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-253"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"f1","text":"The driver of a vehicle","role":"condition"},{"id":"f2","text":"within an intersection","role":"condition"},{"id":"f3","text":"intending to turn to the left","role":"condition"},{"id":"f4","text":"shall yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"f5","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"f6","text":"to any vehicle approaching from the opposite direction","role":"sibling"},{"id":"f7","text":"which is within the intersection","role":"sibling"},{"id":"f8","text":"or so close thereto as to constitute an immediate hazard,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"f9","text":"but such driver,","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"f10","text":"having so yielded","role":"condition"},{"id":"f11","text":"and having given a signal when and as required,","role":"condition"},{"id":"f12","text":"may make such left turn","role":"condition"},{"id":"f13","text":"and the drivers of all other vehicles approaching the intersection from the opposite direction","role":"subject"},{"id":"f14","text":"shall yield","role":"obligation"},{"id":"f15","text":"the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"f16","text":"to the vehicle making the left turn.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"f1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"a vehicle\": the left-turning road user t, other than ego, of the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; \"The driver\" read through its controlled motion."},{"span":"f2","atoms":["st.intersection","rel.occupies"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"within an intersection\": t's footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) the intersection i (st.intersection); i is the region t's intention is declared at."},{"span":"f11","atoms":["sig.turn_indicator","sig.hand_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"having given a signal\": t showed a left signal, its turn indicator state left (sig.turn_indicator, 'the turn indicator state ... left') or an arm signal of meaning left (sig.hand_signal), at some observation since t occupied its approach carrier into i; the signal itself, not a declared intention, and not the turn. \"when and as required\": the timing and manner another statute sets, outside this corpus; the signal is read as given before the judged observation."},{"span":"f12","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.turning_left"],"justification":"\"may make such left turn\": t is making the left turn it intends, drv.motion.turning_left (moving with its heading turning to the left at or above the yaw tolerance), a turn under way rather than one completed."},{"span":"f13","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","st.lane_enters","st.lane_direction","st.travel_region","rel.occupies"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"the drivers of all other vehicles\": ego, a vehicle (admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) other than t, its driver read through its controlled motion. \"approaching the intersection\": ego occupies a carrier c_e whose entrance end is i and does not overlap i, or enters i from it (st.lane_enters, rel.occupies). \"from the opposite direction\": c_e and the carrier from which t entered i carry opposed designated directions (st.lane_direction), as rel.oncoming's contract directs, not the current headings."},{"span":"f14","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"\"shall yield\": granting precedence (DEF-NRS-484A-210 \"unless one grants precedence to the other\"): ego is at rest (drv.motion.at_rest) or not in conflict with t (operationalization of f15)."},{"span":"f16","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.turning_left"],"justification":"\"the vehicle making the left turn\": the same t, turning left (drv.motion.turning_left) at the judged observation."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"f15","standard":"the right-of-way: DEF-NRS-484A-210 \"approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other\"","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_clearance"],"convention":"Traffic-conflict technique: two road users are in conflict where, projected at their current velocities, their centres approach within the time-to-collision horizon and their closest-approach centre distance is below the clearance at which their bodies would touch. Direction, speed and proximity enter by degree through the projected velocities and positions.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[{"span":"f3","id":"int.left_turn","meaning":"The road user's current plan includes turning left at the target region."}],"compositions":[{"span":"f10","rule":"NRS_484B_253_o1","map":{"ego":"t"},"as":"compliance"}],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"Ego is a vehicle (driven: agency reading) approaching an intersection i (on a carrier c_e whose entrance end is i, not overlapping i, or entering i from it), and some vehicle t other than ego overlaps i, declares int.left_turn at i, is turning left (drv.motion.turning_left, p.turn_yaw_tolerance, p.rest_speed_tolerance), showed a left signal (sig.turn_indicator left or sig.hand_signal left) at some observation since it occupied its approach carrier into i, has complied with NRS_484B_253_o1 (t as its ego) at every observation since it entered i, and entered i from a carrier c_t whose direction and c_e's have a dot product below minus p.opposite_direction_tolerance (st.lane_direction).","obligation":"Ego is at rest (drv.motion.at_rest, p.rest_speed_tolerance) or not in conflict with t: not both prim.closest_approach_within(ego, t) with horizon p.conflict_horizon and prim.closest_approach_distance(ego, t) with the same horizon below p.conflict_clearance.","params":["p.rest_speed_tolerance","p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_clearance","p.opposite_direction_tolerance","p.turn_yaw_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"f13","why":"'the drivers' are read through the vehicles' controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Vehicle t, within the intersection with int.left_turn and its left indicator on since its approach, waited while no oncoming vehicle was close and now turns left. Ego approaches from the opposite direction and keeps moving; their projected closest approach lies within p.conflict_horizon below p.conflict_clearance."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; ego slows and comes to rest at the edge of the intersection until t completes its turn."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"t crosses the intersection straight ahead (no int.left_turn, not turning left); ego approaches from the opposite direction."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Scene of forbid, but the source declares sig.turn_indicator and sig.hand_signal absent: whether t signalled cannot be read.","masked":["sig.turn_indicator","sig.hand_signal"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"As forbid, but t's indicator stayed off and it gave no arm signal: t gave no signal, so the opposing drivers' duty does not arise."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"As forbid, but t began its turn while ego was already within the immediate-hazard distance of the intersection: t did not yield as NRS_484B_253_o1 requires, so the duty to yield to it does not arise."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement.","source":"Naturalistic-driving and simulator stop-detection practice (SHRP 2 event coding; CARLA ground-truth velocity resolution)."},{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"Time-to-collision horizon of the traffic-conflict technique.","source":"Hayward (1972) time-to-collision; Hyden (1987) Swedish Traffic Conflict Technique; van der Horst (1990) TTC thresholds."},{"name":"p.conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Centre-to-centre distance at the projected closest approach below which the bodies of two passenger vehicles would touch or nearly touch.","source":"AASHTO Green Book, design vehicle P dimensions."},{"name":"p.opposite_direction_tolerance","unit":"1","value":0.866,"convention":"Cosine of the largest angle off exactly opposed at which two approach directions still count as opposite (thirty degrees).","source":"Trajectory-processing conventions for opposing-movement classification at intersections (inD)."},{"name":"p.turn_yaw_tolerance","unit":"deg/s","value":5.0,"convention":"Yaw rate below which a change of heading counts as none.","source":"Vehicle-dynamics practice for turn-onset detection from yaw-rate sensors."}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_257_1_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-257-1"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"g1","text":"Except when traffic is being controlled by a police officer or a traffic-control signal:","role":"exception"},{"id":"g2","text":"When proper signs have been erected,","role":"condition"},{"id":"g3","text":"the driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"g4","text":"shall stop or yield","role":"obligation"},{"id":"g5","text":"at a clearly marked stop line","role":"condition"},{"id":"g6","text":"or, if there is none, before entering the crosswalk on the near side of the intersection","role":"condition"},{"id":"g7","text":"or, if there is none, then at the point nearest the intersection where the driver has a view of approaching traffic on the through highway.","role":"condition"},{"id":"g8","text":"After having stopped or, in the event of a yield sign, slowed or stopped,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g9","text":"the driver","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g10","text":"shall yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g11","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g12","text":"to other vehicles which have entered the intersection from such through highway","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g13","text":"or which are approaching so closely on such through highway as to constitute an immediate hazard","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g14","text":"during the time such driver is moving across or within the intersection.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"g1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","dev.human_direction","dev.traffic_signal","dev.governs","dev.inoperative"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"traffic\": the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, of which ego, a vehicle using the highway, is a member. \"being controlled by a police officer\": a dev.human_direction of role police_officer ('a person directing traffic and the direction given'; DEF-NRS-484A-180 'every officer authorized to direct or regulate traffic') governing (dev.governs) ego's approach carrier c or the intersection i at ego's entry. \"or a traffic-control signal\": a dev.traffic_signal head governing c or i that is not inoperative (dev.inoperative, 'showing no valid indication', does not hold) at the entry: a dark head controls no traffic."},{"span":"g2","atoms":["dev.stop_sign","dev.yield_sign","dev.governs","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"proper signs\": a stop sign (dev.stop_sign, 'regulatory sign requiring a full halt') or a yield sign (dev.yield_sign, 'regulatory sign requiring yielding without a mandatory halt') governing (dev.governs) ego's approach carrier c, whose entrance end is the intersection i (st.lane_enters); \"proper\" and \"erected\" are the signs' legal status, read through their presence (status reading). A sign is not a signal."},{"span":"g3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"a vehicle\": the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; \"the driver\" read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency reading)."},{"span":"g4","atoms":["kin.path_length"],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest","drv.motion.decelerating"],"justification":"\"stop\": a stop when required, DEF-NRS-484A-255 \"complete cessation from movement\" (DEF-NRS-484A-260 governs a stop 'when prohibited'): drv.motion.at_rest, owed under a stop sign. \"yield\" at the place, under a yield sign alone: the line's own later words state what it is, \"in the event of a yield sign, slowed or stopped\": at rest at the place, or slowed, read as ego decelerating (drv.motion.decelerating, its acceleration along its heading below the negative tolerance) at some observation within the distance window p.yield_slowing_distance travelled before it is within the place's stopping zone, a .path window that reads kin.path_length."},{"span":"g5","atoms":["st.stop_line","st.entrance_of","st.region_geometry","st.lane_direction","prim.region_offset_along"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.stop_line, 'the transverse line marking where vehicles halt for a device', tied to ego's approach carrier c by st.entrance_of, never by distance. \"at\" the line: ego's body within p.stop_point_tolerance of it (st.region_geometry) and not past it, side read along c's designated direction (st.lane_direction, prim.region_offset_along). \"clearly marked\": the represented line is read as the clearly marked one (status reading)."},{"span":"g6","atoms":["st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.region_geometry","rel.occupies","st.lane_direction","prim.region_offset_along"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"if there is none\": the source's list of stop lines marking c is complete and none marks it. \"the crosswalk on the near side\": the st.crosswalk marking c (st.entrance_of). \"before entering\": ego halts short of it with its footprint not overlapping it (rel.occupies false), within p.stop_point_tolerance outside it (st.region_geometry), side read along c (st.lane_direction, prim.region_offset_along)."},{"span":"g7","atoms":["st.intersection","st.region_geometry","rel.occupies","st.lane_enters"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"if there is none\": neither a stop line nor a crosswalk marks c (lists complete). \"then at the point nearest the intersection\": c's entrance end at i (st.lane_enters); the act counts there where ego's footprint does not overlap i (rel.occupies false) and its body lies within p.stop_point_tolerance of i (st.region_geometry). \"where the driver has a view of approaching traffic on the through highway\": a perception, read through the place it secures (perception reading)."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"Ego is a vehicle (driven: agency reading) and the judged observation is an entry of ego into an intersection i (its footprint overlaps i and did not at the observation before, when it occupied a carrier c whose entrance end is i; st.lane_enters) where a stop sign or a yield sign governs c (dev.stop_sign, dev.yield_sign, dev.governs); not where, at that entry, a police officer directs (dev.human_direction role police_officer governing c or i) or a traffic signal head governing c or i is not inoperative (dev.traffic_signal, dev.inoperative).","obligation":"Event and target: the entry of ego into i through c. Place: the stop line marking c (st.stop_line, st.entrance_of) where one is recorded; else, where the source's list for c is complete and no stop line marks it, the crosswalk marking c, the act there being short of it with ego's footprint not overlapping it; else the entrance end of c at i, outside i. Act: where a stop sign governs c, a halt, ego at rest (drv.motion.at_rest, p.rest_speed_tolerance) on c with its body within p.stop_point_tolerance of the place (st.region_geometry) and not past it, side read along c's designated direction (st.lane_direction, sign of prim.region_offset_along); where only a yield sign governs c, that halt, or an observation at which ego, on c, is within the place's stopping zone and not past the place and had decelerated (drv.motion.decelerating, p.decel_tolerance, p.rest_speed_tolerance) at some observation of the .path window of length p.yield_slowing_distance behind it. Search: from the entry back to the approach start, the last observation before the entry at which ego, on a carrier the place marks, is outside the place's stopping zone upstream (off the place, short of it along c's direction and farther from it than p.stop_point_tolerance), or back to ego's previous entry into i, whichever comes first; nothing else ends it, not the start of the recording, not ego's first observation, not a distance travelled. Only an observed exit from the stopping zone upstream begins a new approach; crossing the place, a lateral move, a change of carrier within the same entry or a reverse within the zone does not, and none loses an act already done. Verdict: compliant where the search finds the act; violated where it reaches the approach start or the previous entry without it; unknown where it reaches neither (the approach began before the recording), where whether the entry occurred is unknown, where which place governs turns on an unobserved association or an incomplete list, or where the sign's governance of c is unobserved.","params":["p.rest_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance","p.decel_tolerance","p.yield_slowing_distance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"g3","why":"'the driver' is read through ego's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"g2","why":"'proper' and 'erected' are read through the presence of the stop or yield sign governing ego's approach.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"g5","why":"'clearly marked' is read through the presence of the represented stop line; the paint's clarity is not modelled.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"g7","why":"'where the driver has a view of approaching traffic on the through highway' is read through the place it secures: the entrance end of ego's approach carrier, outside the intersection.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"perception"},{"span":"g4","why":"'yield' at the place under a yield sign is read as the line's own words state it, 'slowed or stopped'; 'slowed' is read as a deceleration within a distance window before the stopping zone, not as a reduction to any particular speed.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A stop sign governs ego's approach lane c and a stop line marks c; no officer and no signal. Ego approaches from beyond the stopping zone and enters the intersection without being at rest at any observation since the approach start."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; ego comes to rest within p.stop_point_tolerance of the line, short of it, then enters."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"No stop sign or yield sign governs ego's approach; ego enters an intersection whose approaches carry no signs."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Scene of forbid, but the source declares dev.governs absent: whether the stop sign governs ego's approach cannot be read.","masked":["dev.governs"]},{"name":"history_boundary","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Stop sign governs c, stop line marks c. The recording begins with ego already within the stopping zone of the line moving slowly; ego enters without being at rest at any recorded observation; the approach start precedes the recording and no previous entry is recorded.","boundary":"the approach start: the observation at which ego, on c, was last outside the stop line's stopping zone upstream, which precedes the recording"},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Only a yield sign governs c. Ego decelerates on the approach within p.yield_slowing_distance before the stopping zone of the line and enters without stopping."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A stop sign governs c, but at ego's entry a police officer (dev.human_direction role police_officer) directs traffic at the intersection."},{"name":"branch_3","expected":"violated","narrative":"Only a yield sign governs c. Ego keeps a constant speed from beyond the stopping zone into the intersection, never decelerating and never at rest."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement.","source":"Naturalistic-driving and simulator stop-detection practice (SHRP 2 event coding; CARLA ground-truth velocity resolution)."},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Stop-point tolerance of the ontology's approach convention: the body-to-mark distance within which an act counts as made at the mark.","source":"MUTCD (2009) Section 3B.16 stop line placement; positioning accuracy of stop-compliance studies."},{"name":"p.decel_tolerance","unit":"m/s²","value":0.5,"convention":"Longitudinal deceleration below which a sampled acceleration counts as none: above coasting and sensor noise, below deliberate braking.","source":"Naturalistic-driving braking-event detection practice (SHRP 2; 100-Car study)."},{"name":"p.yield_slowing_distance","unit":"m","value":30.0,"convention":"Distance travelled before the stopping zone within which a slowing for a yield sign counts as made for that sign: the braking distance of an urban approach.","source":"AASHTO Green Book stopping sight distance at urban approach speeds."}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_257_1_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-257-1"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"g1","text":"Except when traffic is being controlled by a police officer or a traffic-control signal:","role":"exception"},{"id":"g2","text":"When proper signs have been erected,","role":"condition"},{"id":"g3","text":"the driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"g4","text":"shall stop or yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g5","text":"at a clearly marked stop line","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g6","text":"or, if there is none, before entering the crosswalk on the near side of the intersection","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g7","text":"or, if there is none, then at the point nearest the intersection where the driver has a view of approaching traffic on the through highway.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g8","text":"After having stopped or, in the event of a yield sign, slowed or stopped,","role":"condition"},{"id":"g9","text":"the driver","role":"subject"},{"id":"g10","text":"shall yield","role":"obligation"},{"id":"g11","text":"the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"g12","text":"to other vehicles which have entered the intersection from such through highway","role":"condition"},{"id":"g13","text":"or which are approaching so closely on such through highway as to constitute an immediate hazard","role":"standard"},{"id":"g14","text":"during the time such driver is moving across or within the intersection.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"g1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","dev.human_direction","dev.traffic_signal","dev.governs","dev.inoperative"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"traffic\": the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, of which ego is a member. \"being controlled by a police officer\": a dev.human_direction of role police_officer governing (dev.governs) ego's approach carrier c or the intersection i at ego's entry. \"or a traffic-control signal\": a dev.traffic_signal head governing c or i that is not inoperative (dev.inoperative) at the entry."},{"span":"g2","atoms":["dev.stop_sign","dev.yield_sign","dev.governs","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"proper signs\": a stop sign (dev.stop_sign) or a yield sign (dev.yield_sign) governing (dev.governs) ego's approach carrier c, whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters); status read through presence."},{"span":"g3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"a vehicle\": the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; \"the driver\" read through its controlled motion (agency reading)."},{"span":"g8","atoms":["dev.stop_sign","dev.yield_sign","st.stop_line","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.region_geometry","rel.occupies","st.lane_direction","prim.region_offset_along","kin.path_length"],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest","drv.motion.decelerating"],"justification":"The referent is the act g4-g7 require on ego's approach c to i, carried in full: under a stop sign (dev.stop_sign), \"having stopped\" at the governing place (the stop line marking c, st.stop_line and st.entrance_of; else short of the crosswalk marking c, st.crosswalk and rel.occupies false; else outside i at c's entrance end), ego at rest (drv.motion.at_rest, DEF-NRS-484A-255 \"complete cessation from movement\") with its body within p.stop_point_tolerance of the place (st.region_geometry), side read along c (st.lane_direction, prim.region_offset_along); \"in the event of a yield sign\" (dev.yield_sign), \"slowed or stopped\": that halt, or ego within the place's stopping zone having decelerated (drv.motion.decelerating) within the .path window p.yield_slowing_distance behind (kin.path_length); found between the approach start and ego's entry into i, as NRS_484B_257_1_o1 states. \"After\": the judged observations follow that act."},{"span":"g9","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"the driver\": of ego, a vehicle (admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), read through its controlled motion (agency reading)."},{"span":"g10","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"\"shall yield\": granting precedence (DEF-NRS-484A-210 \"unless one grants precedence to the other\"): ego is at rest (drv.motion.at_rest) or not in conflict with the vehicle it yields to (operationalization of g11)."},{"span":"g12","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.on_way","st.highway","dev.stop_sign","dev.yield_sign","dev.governs"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"other vehicles\": road users b other than ego of the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle. \"have entered the intersection\": b's footprint overlaps i (rel.occupies) after an entry from a carrier c_b whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters), read through a past operator. \"such through highway\" (DEF-NRS-484A-275: \"on which vehicular traffic is given the right-of-way, and at the entrances to which vehicular traffic from intersecting highways is required by law to yield\"): c_b lies (st.on_way) on a highway (st.highway) on which ego's carrier c does not lie, and no stop sign or yield sign governs c_b (dev.stop_sign, dev.yield_sign, dev.governs): traffic on it is given the right-of-way while ego's entrance yields."},{"span":"g14","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"\"during the time such driver is moving across or within the intersection\": ego's footprint overlaps i (rel.occupies) and ego is not at rest (drv.motion.at_rest does not hold); the duty is judged at those observations."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"g11","standard":"the right-of-way: DEF-NRS-484A-210 \"approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other\"","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_clearance"],"convention":"Traffic-conflict technique: two road users are in conflict where, projected at their current velocities, their centres approach within the time-to-collision horizon and their closest-approach centre distance is below the clearance at which their bodies would touch. Direction, speed and proximity enter by degree through the projected velocities and positions.","surrogate":false},{"span":"g13","standard":"approaching so closely on such through highway as to constitute an immediate hazard","concepts":["st.region_geometry","kin.speed","st.lane_enters","st.on_way","rel.occupies"],"params":["p.immediate_hazard_time"],"convention":"Gap acceptance: a vehicle b on a carrier c_b of the through highway whose entrance end is i (st.lane_enters, st.on_way, rel.occupies) is an immediate hazard during ego's crossing where its time to reach the intersection is below the critical headway, read as the ground distance from its body to i (st.region_geometry) at or below its speed (kin.speed) times the critical headway; distance and speed enter by degree.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"Ego is a vehicle (driven: agency reading) that entered an intersection i from a carrier c (st.lane_enters) governed by a stop sign or a yield sign (dev.stop_sign, dev.yield_sign, dev.governs), where at that entry no police officer directed (dev.human_direction role police_officer governing c or i) and no traffic signal head governing c or i was operating (dev.traffic_signal, dev.inoperative); and that made on c, between the approach start and that entry, the act g8 names (under a stop sign a halt at the governing place; under a yield sign alone that halt or a deceleration within p.yield_slowing_distance before the place's stopping zone; drv.motion.at_rest, drv.motion.decelerating, p.rest_speed_tolerance, p.decel_tolerance, p.stop_point_tolerance). Judged at every observation from that entry at which ego overlaps i and is not at rest. Where the history that act's search needs precedes the recording, the applicability is unknown.","obligation":"For every vehicle b other than ego that either overlaps i after an entry from a carrier c_b of the through highway (c_b lies on a highway on which c does not lie, and no stop sign or yield sign governs c_b), or occupies such a carrier c_b whose entrance end is i with the ground distance from its body to i (st.region_geometry) at or below its speed (kin.speed) times p.immediate_hazard_time: ego is not in conflict with b, that is not both prim.closest_approach_within(ego, b) with horizon p.conflict_horizon and prim.closest_approach_distance(ego, b) with the same horizon below p.conflict_clearance.","params":["p.rest_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance","p.decel_tolerance","p.yield_slowing_distance","p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_clearance","p.immediate_hazard_time"],"narrowings":[{"span":"g3","why":"'the driver' is read through ego's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"g2","why":"'proper' and 'erected' are read through the presence of the stop or yield sign governing ego's approach.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A stop sign governs ego's approach c; ego comes to rest at the stop line marking c, then crosses the intersection while vehicle b approaches on the unsigned through highway at a distance from the intersection below its speed times p.immediate_hazard_time; their projected closest approach lies within p.conflict_horizon below p.conflict_clearance while ego is within the intersection."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; ego stays at rest at the line until b has passed, then crosses with no projected conflict."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"No stop or yield sign governs ego's approach; ego crosses the intersection."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Scene of forbid, but the source declares dev.governs absent: whether the stop sign governs ego's approach cannot be read.","masked":["dev.governs"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"As forbid, except that ego's only halt was far upstream of the stop line, outside its stopping zone, and ego did not halt at the line: the act g8 refers to was not made, so this duty does not arise (NRS_484B_257_1_o1 judges the missing halt)."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A stop sign governs c; ego stops at the line and crosses with no other road user in the scene."},{"name":"branch_3","expected":"violated","narrative":"Only a yield sign governs c; ego decelerates before the line, enters without stopping, and is in projected conflict with vehicle b that had already entered the intersection from the through highway."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement.","source":"Naturalistic-driving and simulator stop-detection practice (SHRP 2 event coding; CARLA ground-truth velocity resolution)."},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Stop-point tolerance of the ontology's approach convention: the body-to-mark distance within which an act counts as made at the mark.","source":"MUTCD (2009) Section 3B.16 stop line placement; positioning accuracy of stop-compliance studies."},{"name":"p.decel_tolerance","unit":"m/s²","value":0.5,"convention":"Longitudinal deceleration below which a sampled acceleration counts as none.","source":"Naturalistic-driving braking-event detection practice (SHRP 2; 100-Car study)."},{"name":"p.yield_slowing_distance","unit":"m","value":30.0,"convention":"Distance travelled before the stopping zone within which a slowing for a yield sign counts as made for that sign.","source":"AASHTO Green Book stopping sight distance at urban approach speeds."},{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"Time-to-collision horizon of the traffic-conflict technique.","source":"Hayward (1972) time-to-collision; Hyden (1987) Swedish Traffic Conflict Technique; van der Horst (1990) TTC thresholds."},{"name":"p.conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Centre-to-centre distance at the projected closest approach below which the bodies of two passenger vehicles would touch or nearly touch.","source":"AASHTO Green Book, design vehicle P dimensions."},{"name":"p.immediate_hazard_time","unit":"s","value":4.1,"convention":"Critical headway of gap acceptance: an approaching vehicle whose time to reach the intersection is below it is too close for a crossing manoeuvre to be completed ahead of it.","source":"Highway Capacity Manual, 6th ed., base critical headways for two-way stop-controlled intersections."}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.at_rest","kind":"formula","contract":"A road user is at rest at an observation: the observable form of a stop where one is required, \"complete cessation from movement\". It holds at each observation at which the road user's speed (kin.speed, m/s) is at or below the speed tolerance, the speed at or below which a sampled measurement counts as no movement, and at no other. Not a stand-in for the brake lamp or the brake input, which are actuations and not motion, or for a halt at a particular place, which a caller states with its own relations.","definition":"DEF-NRS-484A-255","args":[{"name":"a","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","meaning":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement"}],"elements":[{"span":"the road user's speed (kin.speed, m/s) is at or below the speed tolerance","atoms":["kin.speed"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.speed: 'magnitude of velocity' in m/s; a magnitude at or below the tolerance is no movement within the measurement's resolution. It reads motion, not the brake lamp (sig.brake_lamp 'Not a stand-in for: a halt')."}],"residues":[{"span":"when required","why":"The definition's 'when required' names the occasion a calling rule fixes (where and before what the stop is owed), not a property of the motion."}],"literals":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A vehicle's kin.speed reads zero at the observation."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"A vehicle's kin.speed is well above the speed tolerance while its brake lamp is lit."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The source declares kin.speed absent.","masked":["kin.speed"]}],"used_by":["LVMC_11_30_030","NRS_484B_113_3","NRS_484B_117_1","NRS_484B_250_4_o1","NRS_484B_250_4_o2","NRS_484B_250_1","NRS_484B_253_o1","NRS_484B_253_o2","NRS_484B_257_1_o1","NRS_484B_257_1_o2"],"supersedes":null}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.backing","kind":"formula","contract":"A road user is backing at an observation: it moves in the direction opposite to the one its body points. Measured as the component of its velocity (kin.velocity, m/s, world frame) along its heading (kin.heading, unit vector) lying below the negative of the motion tolerance, the speed below which a sampled motion counts as none. Not a stand-in for the gear selected: a vehicle in reverse gear that stands still or rolls forward is not backing, and one in a forward gear that rolls backwards is.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"a","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"motion_tolerance","unit":"m/s","meaning":"the speed below which a sampled motion along the heading counts as none"}],"elements":[{"span":"the component of its velocity (kin.velocity, m/s, world frame) along its heading (kin.heading, unit vector)","atoms":["kin.velocity","kin.heading"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.velocity 'velocity vector' and kin.heading 'direction the body points': their product along the heading is negative when the body moves rearward. kin.gear is not read: its contract says it is 'Not a stand-in for: the direction of motion'."}],"residues":[],"literals":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A vehicle's velocity points opposite its heading at a speed above the motion tolerance."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"A vehicle in reverse gear stands still."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The source declares kin.velocity absent.","masked":["kin.velocity"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_113_3"],"supersedes":null}
{"concept_id":"drv.position.near_region","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user a is at region r at an observation: r lies within the reach of a's body, the distance within which a region counts as the place the road user is at. Measured as the ground distance from a's body outline to r (st.region_geometry, m; zero when they overlap) at or below the reach. Not a stand-in for occupancy: a body within the reach may lie wholly outside the region.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"a","sort":"track"},{"name":"r","sort":"region"}],"params":[{"name":"reach","unit":"m","meaning":"the ground distance from the body within which a region counts as the place the road user is at"}],"elements":[{"span":"the ground distance from a's body outline to r (st.region_geometry, m; zero when they overlap)","atoms":["st.region_geometry"],"concepts":[],"justification":"st.region_geometry: 'the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it (zero when they overlap)'; its 'Not a stand-in for: occupancy' is respected: the concept states nearness, never overlap."}],"residues":[],"literals":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A vehicle stands with its front a short distance before a crosswalk, within the reach."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"A vehicle stands far beyond the reach from the crosswalk."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The source maps the crosswalk without its outline and declares st.region_geometry absent.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]}],"used_by":["LVMC_11_30_030"],"supersedes":null}
{"concept_id":"drv.position.behind","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user a is behind road user b at an observation: their headings are aligned and b's body lies wholly ahead of a's along a's heading. Measured as headings aligned (rel.same_direction with the alignment tolerance, the cosine of the largest angle between the headings counted as aligned), the bearing of b from a (rel.bearing) pointing forward in a's frame, and the two footprints' projections on a's heading sharing no length (rel.longitudinal_overlap below zero). Either road user may be at rest. Not a stand-in for following in the same lane: b may travel in another lane.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"a","sort":"track"},{"name":"b","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"alignment","unit":"1","meaning":"the cosine of the largest angle between the two headings counted as aligned"}],"elements":[{"span":"headings aligned (rel.same_direction with the alignment tolerance, the cosine of the largest angle between the headings counted as aligned)","atoms":["rel.same_direction"],"concepts":[],"justification":"rel.same_direction: 'headings aligned: the cosine of the angle between the headings is above its tolerance'."},{"span":"the bearing of b from a (rel.bearing) pointing forward in a's frame","atoms":["rel.bearing"],"concepts":[],"justification":"rel.bearing: 'direction of b from a in a's frame (for ... \"immediately to the rear\")'; a forward component tells ahead from behind, which the overlap alone does not."},{"span":"the two footprints' projections on a's heading sharing no length (rel.longitudinal_overlap below zero)","atoms":["rel.longitudinal_overlap"],"concepts":[],"justification":"rel.longitudinal_overlap: 'the length the two footprints' projections on that axis share, negative for the gap between the projections'; it is a projection, so it is used for 'wholly ahead' and never as a distance or a contact. rel.ahead_behind_in_lane is not read, since it holds only within one lane."}],"residues":[],"literals":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"a travels in the left lane with a gap between its front and the rear of b, which is at rest in the right lane, headings aligned."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"a is alongside b: their projections on a's heading share a length."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The source declares rel.longitudinal_overlap absent.","masked":["rel.longitudinal_overlap"]}],"used_by":["LVMC_11_30_030"],"supersedes":null}
{"concept_id":"drv.interaction.overtakes","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user a overtakes and passes road user b: travelling with headings aligned, a goes from wholly behind b to wholly ahead of it. The act is recognized at the observation at which a becomes wholly ahead of b, that is, at which drv.position.behind of b relative to a becomes true, provided that a was behind b (drv.position.behind of a relative to b) at an earlier observation and the headings stayed aligned (rel.same_direction with the alignment tolerance) at every observation from that one to the recognition. Its observed beginning is the last observation at which a was behind b before the recognition. The concept holds at the recognition observation only. Where the recording shows no observation of a behind b before a becomes wholly ahead of it, with the headings aligned at every observation since the recording began, whether a overtook b is unknown, never false. Not a stand-in for a lane change or for contact between the bodies; it does not say in which lane either travels.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"a","sort":"track"},{"name":"b","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"alignment","unit":"1","meaning":"the cosine of the largest angle between the two headings counted as aligned"}],"act":{"boundary":"event","onset":"Its observed beginning is the last observation at which a was behind b before the recognition.","recognition":"The act is recognized at the observation at which a becomes wholly ahead of b","extent":"The concept holds at the recognition observation only.","history":"Where the recording shows no observation of a behind b before a becomes wholly ahead of it, with the headings aligned at every observation since the recording began, whether a overtook b is unknown, never false."},"elements":[{"span":"drv.position.behind of b relative to a becomes true","concepts":["drv.position.behind"],"atoms":[],"justification":"drv.position.behind states one road user wholly behind the other with aligned headings; read both ways it gives the beginning (a behind b) and the recognition (b behind a)."},{"span":"the headings stayed aligned (rel.same_direction with the alignment tolerance)","atoms":["rel.same_direction"],"concepts":[],"justification":"rel.same_direction: 'headings aligned: the cosine of the angle between the headings is above its tolerance'; held at every observation from the beginning to the recognition, so an oncoming crossing is no pass."}],"residues":[],"literals":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"a, in the left lane wholly behind b with aligned headings, comes alongside and becomes wholly ahead of b; the concept holds at that observation."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"a comes alongside b and stays alongside to the end of the recording, never wholly ahead."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The source declares rel.longitudinal_overlap absent.","masked":["rel.longitudinal_overlap"]}],"used_by":["LVMC_11_30_030"],"supersedes":null}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.left_turn","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user a makes a left turn: within the window behind the observation its heading turns to the left by an angle within the turn band, from the lower bound, below which a heading change counts as no turn, up to the upper bound, above which the road user's direction counts as reversed. Measured as the signed heading change over the window (prim.heading_change, degrees, left positive) at or above the lower bound and at or below the upper bound. The act is recognized at the observation at which the heading change over the window first reaches the lower bound. Its observed beginning lies within the window behind that observation. The concept holds at every observation at which the heading change over the window lies within the band, and ends where it leaves the band. It is unknown where the window reaches past the start of the recording or a yaw rate in it is missing. Not a stand-in for the turn indicator or for a declared intention to turn.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"a","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"window","unit":"s","meaning":"the window behind the observation within which the turn is completed"},{"name":"min_angle","unit":"deg","meaning":"the leftward heading change below which a change counts as no turn"},{"name":"max_angle","unit":"deg","meaning":"the leftward heading change above which the direction counts as reversed"}],"act":{"boundary":"window","window":"window","onset":"Its observed beginning lies within the window behind that observation.","recognition":"The act is recognized at the observation at which the heading change over the window first reaches the lower bound.","extent":"The concept holds at every observation at which the heading change over the window lies within the band, and ends where it leaves the band.","history":"It is unknown where the window reaches past the start of the recording or a yaw rate in it is missing."},"elements":[{"span":"the signed heading change over the window (prim.heading_change, degrees, left positive)","atoms":["prim.heading_change"],"concepts":[],"justification":"prim.heading_change: 'the signed heading change (degrees, left positive) of a road user over the window behind the observation'; it reads the body's heading, not the turn indicator."}],"residues":[],"literals":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Within the window a vehicle's heading turns left by an angle inside the band."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"A vehicle changes lane to the left; its heading changes by less than the lower bound."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The source declares kin.yaw_rate absent.","masked":["kin.yaw_rate"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_227_1_o3"],"supersedes":null}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.u_turn","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user a makes a U-turn: \"the turning of a vehicle upon a highway so as to proceed in the opposite direction, whether accomplished by one continuous movement or not\". Observed as a heading change within the window behind the observation, to either hand, whose magnitude lies within the reversal band: from the lower bound, at or beyond which the road user's direction counts as reversed, up to the upper bound, beyond which it has turned past the opposite direction. Measured as the magnitude of the signed heading change over the window (prim.heading_change, degrees). The window admits a turn made in several movements, forward and reverse. The act is recognized at the observation at which the magnitude first reaches the lower bound. Its observed beginning lies within the window behind that observation. The concept holds at every observation at which the magnitude lies within the band, and ends where it leaves the band. It is unknown where the window reaches past the start of the recording or a yaw rate in it is missing. Not a stand-in for backing: a reversal of travel without a change of heading is no U-turn.","definition":"DEF-NRS-484B-077","args":[{"name":"a","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"window","unit":"s","meaning":"the window behind the observation within which the turn, in one movement or several, is completed"},{"name":"min_angle","unit":"deg","meaning":"the heading change at or beyond which the direction counts as reversed"},{"name":"max_angle","unit":"deg","meaning":"the heading change beyond which the road user has turned past the opposite direction"}],"act":{"boundary":"window","window":"window","onset":"Its observed beginning lies within the window behind that observation.","recognition":"The act is recognized at the observation at which the magnitude first reaches the lower bound.","extent":"The concept holds at every observation at which the magnitude lies within the band, and ends where it leaves the band.","history":"It is unknown where the window reaches past the start of the recording or a yaw rate in it is missing."},"elements":[{"span":"the magnitude of the signed heading change over the window (prim.heading_change, degrees)","atoms":["prim.heading_change"],"concepts":[],"justification":"prim.heading_change: 'the signed heading change (degrees, left positive) of a road user over the window behind the observation, integrated from kin.yaw_rate'; integrated over the window it sums every movement of a multi-point turn, forward and reverse."}],"residues":[{"span":"upon a highway","why":"The place of the turn is read by the calling rule, which binds the region."},{"span":"of a vehicle","why":"The class of the road user is the calling rule's: a is whatever road user it passes."}],"literals":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A vehicle reverses its direction by a forward, a reverse and a forward movement within the window; the magnitude of its heading change reaches the band."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"A vehicle backs along the road with no change of heading."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The source declares kin.yaw_rate absent.","masked":["kin.yaw_rate"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_227_1_o3"],"supersedes":null}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.turning_left","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user a is turning to the left at an observation: it moves and its heading turns to the left. Measured as a not at rest (drv.motion.at_rest with the speed tolerance does not hold) and its yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate, deg/s, left positive) at or above the yaw tolerance, the rate below which a change of heading counts as none. A state at each observation while a turn is under way, not a completed manoeuvre: it does not say how far the turn goes, and it holds alike where the road user follows a bend of the road to the left. Not a stand-in for the turn indicator or for a declared intention to turn.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"a","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"yaw_tolerance","unit":"deg/s","meaning":"the yaw rate below which a change of heading counts as none"},{"name":"speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","meaning":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement"}],"elements":[{"span":"a not at rest (drv.motion.at_rest with the speed tolerance does not hold)","atoms":[],"concepts":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"drv.motion.at_rest states no movement; its negation is a moving road user, so a vehicle turning its wheels on the spot is not turning."},{"span":"its yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate, deg/s, left positive)","atoms":["kin.yaw_rate"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.yaw_rate: 'rate of change of heading, positive when the heading turns to the left'; it is not road curvature, and the contract says the concept holds alike on a bend."}],"residues":[],"literals":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A moving vehicle's yaw rate is leftward above the tolerance."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"A moving vehicle drives straight with a yaw rate near zero."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The source declares kin.yaw_rate absent.","masked":["kin.yaw_rate"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_250_1","NRS_484B_253_o2"],"supersedes":null}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.decelerating","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user a is decelerating at an observation: its forward speed is falling. Measured as its acceleration along its heading (kin.accel_longitudinal, m/s², signed) at or below the negative of the deceleration tolerance, the magnitude below which a sampled acceleration counts as none, while a is not backing (drv.motion.backing with the speed tolerance does not hold), since for a backing road user a negative value is a gain of speed. Not a stand-in for its speed or for the brake lamp: a lit lamp without a deceleration is no deceleration.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"a","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"decel_tolerance","unit":"m/s²","meaning":"the deceleration magnitude below which a sampled acceleration counts as none"},{"name":"speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","meaning":"the speed below which a sampled motion along the heading counts as none"}],"elements":[{"span":"its acceleration along its heading (kin.accel_longitudinal, m/s², signed)","atoms":["kin.accel_longitudinal"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.accel_longitudinal: 'acceleration along heading, signed', 'Not a stand-in for: speed'; a value below the negative tolerance is a falling forward speed."},{"span":"while a is not backing (drv.motion.backing with the speed tolerance does not hold)","atoms":[],"concepts":["drv.motion.backing"],"justification":"drv.motion.backing tells a rearward motion, for which the sign of the acceleration along the heading means the opposite."}],"residues":[],"literals":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A vehicle moving forward brakes; its longitudinal acceleration is below the negative tolerance."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"A vehicle moves forward at constant speed with its brake lamp lit."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The source declares kin.accel_longitudinal absent.","masked":["kin.accel_longitudinal"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_257_1_o1","NRS_484B_257_1_o2"],"supersedes":null}

